    <tr><td>Eviction</td><td><code>allkeys-lru</code>, 5 samples</td><td>Every key is a cache entry; memory binds only if traffic or the catalogue grows</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Client</td><td>One <code>MGET</code> per page; timeouts of a few milliseconds; library retries off; a timed-out lease or lock counts as not held by us</td><td>One round trip; a slow Redis costs a miss, not a pile-up or a false "someone else holds it"</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Topology</td><td>One primary, one replica, three Sentinels; no persistence; no automatic restart; no cluster</td><td>A failover costs 6 seconds; an empty restart costs hours</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Failure plan</td><td>Circuit breaker; database limit of 60 with checkout first; degraded pages; new key versions read the old key first; no <code>FLUSHALL</code></td><td>The cache will be lost or emptied; the limit is the one protection that covers every case</td></tr>
